Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(process): MCP issues carry area:mcp and P1

AGENTS.md "Commands ship with an MCP tool" now says every MCP issue
(an `MCP:` title, or work on the MCP server or the camcraft-mcp skill)
carries `area:mcp` and is P1. The camcraft-mcp skill's two quotes of
that rule match. PROCESS_VERSION 4 -> 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .claude/PROCESS_VERSION              | 2 +-
 .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md | 4 ++--
 AGENTS.md                            | 5 ++++-
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION b/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
index b8626c4c..7ed6ff82 100644
--- a/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
+++ b/.claude/PROCESS_VERSION
@@ -1 +1 @@
-4
+5
diff --git a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
index ff8b86bc..add83f78 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -139,11 +139,11 @@ The following capabilities exist in the GUI or app command layer but do not yet
 8. **Live Interactive GUI Connection (#183, #567):**
    - `camcraft-cli mcp` currently runs as a standalone headless stdio session. Driving an already-running visible GUI window over a live socket is an open enhancement.
 
-*Note:* Several remaining gaps above are tracked under dedicated milestone and feature issues (e.g. #183 live GUI, #258 program headers, #370 tool body alignment, #511 feature recognition). Per `AGENTS.md`, any future command PR that does not bundle an MCP tool must file a corresponding `source:agent` issue titled `MCP: <command>`.
+*Note:* Several remaining gaps above are tracked under dedicated milestone and feature issues (e.g. #183 live GUI, #258 program headers, #370 tool body alignment, #511 feature recognition). Per `AGENTS.md`, any future command PR that does not bundle an MCP tool must file a corresponding `source:agent` issue titled `MCP: <command>`, labelled `P1` and `area:mcp`.
 
 ---
 
 ## Rule for Contributors
 
 Per `AGENTS.md` ("Everything Is a Command"):
-> A PR that adds a user-facing command also adds its MCP tool (and script verb where it fits) in `crates/app/src/mcp/`, or files a `source:agent` follow-up issue `MCP: <command>` and names it in the PR body.
+> A PR that adds a user-facing command also adds its MCP tool (and script verb where it fits) in `crates/app/src/mcp/`, or files a `source:agent` follow-up issue `MCP: <command>` (labels `P1`, `area:mcp`) and names it in the PR body.
diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 04b5c2fc..3a18f6c3 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -381,7 +381,10 @@ If a UI change has no command for it, that's a bug - add one.
 **Commands ship with an MCP tool** (#128, #356). The MCP server lets an AI agent
 drive CamCraft headlessly. A PR that adds a user-facing command also adds its
 MCP tool (and script verb where it fits) in `crates/app/src/mcp/`, or files a
-`source:agent` follow-up issue `MCP: <command>` and names it in the PR body. MCP
+`source:agent` follow-up issue `MCP: <command>` and names it in the PR body. Every
+MCP issue (an `MCP:` title, or work on `crates/app/src/mcp/` or the camcraft-mcp
+skill) carries `area:mcp` and is `P1` (user, 2026-11-10: "find all MCP tickets
+and make P1"), so the agent surface keeps up with the GUI. MCP
 tools call the same undoable commands the GUI uses, so undo/redo history and
 invariants hold headlessly.
 

